    "summaryAr": "About Us At LangChain, our mission is to make intelligent agents ubiquitous. We build the foundation for agent engineering in the real world, helping developers move from prototypes to production-ready AI agents that teams can rely on. We began as widely adopted open-source tools and have grown to also offer a platform for building, evaluating, deploying, and operating agents at scale. With $125M raised at Series B f",
    "descriptionAr": "About Us At LangChain, our mission is to make intelligent agents ubiquitous. We build the foundation for agent engineering in the real world, helping developers move from prototypes to production-ready AI agents that teams can rely on. We began as widely adopted open-source tools and have grown to also offer a platform for building, evaluating, deploying, and operating agents at scale. With $125M raised at Series B from IVP, Sequoia, Benchmark, CapitalG, and Sapphire Ventures, we’re at a stage where we’re continuing to develop new products, growth is accelerating, and all team members have meaningful impact on what we build and how we work together. LangChain is a place where your contributions can shape how this technology shows up in the real world. Today, our platform includes LangSmith (Observability, Evaluation, Deployment, Fleet, and Sandboxes), our open source frameworks (LangChain, LangGraph, and Deep Agents), and the newly launched LangSmith Engine for autonomous agent improvement. We have 100M+ monthly open source downloads, 6,000+ active LangSmith customers, and 5 of the Fortune 10 use LangSmith in production (+ 35% of the Fortune 500 overall), including teams at Klarna, Clay, Coinbase, Workday, Lyft, Cloudflare, Harvey, Rippling, Vanta, LinkedIn, Monday.com, Nvidia, and Bridgewater. About the role We're hiring a Regional Vice President to own and lead our APAC business. You'll inherit a team of four quota-carrying enterprise AEs across Australia, Singapore and be responsible for building the management layer, operating model, and partner ecosystem that takes APAC from early traction to consistent, scaled revenue. This is a Director-level hire with second-line ambition. You'll report directly to the Global Vice President of Sales and operate with meaningful autonomy across pipeline, hiring, partner relationships, and executive engagement. What you'll own Team leadership and performance Lead, develop and expand the Enterprise Sales teams across the APAC region Run weekly pipeline reviews, deal coaching sessions, and forecast calls with precision and consistency Identify and close performance gaps early: coach the team to close larger deals faster and navigate complex, multi-stakeholder cycles Build a culture of accountability and development; create clear career paths for senior individual contributors, including first-line management opportunities as the team scales Revenue Own the APAC number: quarterly and annual quota attainment across all three sub-regions Build and maintain a healthy pipeline that supports consistent delivery and predictable forecasting to Global VP of Sales and leadership Engage directly in strategic deals as executive sponsor, bringing credibility and commercial weight to enterprise negotiations Establish the region's strongest lighthouse accounts across key industry verticals, building referenceable wins that anchor LangChain's market position in APAC Hiring Manage multiple open roles across APAC simultaneously: owning the full hiring lifecycle across pipeline, assessment, and closing Partner with the retained search firm and internal talent team to move at pace without compromising on quality Define the headcount profile for APAC beyond Q4 and feed into H1 planning, ensuring the team is built ahead of the revenue curve Partner ecosystem Owns hyperscaler and GSI/RSI relationships (AWS, Google Cloud, Azure, and key SIs) across APAC Develop a structured partner motion that generates qualified pipeline and supports deal acceleration, reduces risk and drives expansion Represent LangChain at partner QBRs and executive engagements in region Market presence Represent LangChain as a keynote-ready leader at partner events, customer engagements, and industry conferences across the region Build LangChain's brand with technical buyers, CIOs, and innovation leaders across APAC's most important enterprise accounts Bring intelligence on the APAC markets back to the Global VP of Sales and product teams to inform roadmap and go-to-market positioning What we're looking for Experience 8+ years in enterprise SaaS sales, with at least 3 years in a regional or sub-regional leadership role managing quota-carrying AEs Demonstrable track record of hitting and exceeding regional revenue targets across multiple quarters Experience managing teams across multiple countries and time zones, with the cultural intelligence to operate across the APAC region Background selling to technical buyers (engineering leaders, CTOs, platform teams): you understand how developer tools get evaluated and adopted Experience in the AI, data, or developer tooling space strongly preferred; familiarity with the LangChain ecosystem is a meaningful plus Leadership You've run teams of 6+ AEs before and know the difference between managing and coaching You can hold a forecast conversation with a VP and a deal coaching session with an AE in the same afternoon, and add value in both You hire well and fast. You know what good looks like for enterprise AE profiles and you can run structured hiring processes across four open roles simultaneously You've built or contributed to a partner motion before: you understand what \"partner pipeline\" means in practice, not just in theory Operating style You bias toward action. You don't wait for a playbook to be handed to you: you build it You're comfortable with ambiguity and early-stage scale. This is not a role with a fully defined motion; you'll shape a significant part of it You communicate clearly and directly, to your team and to leadership You're present in the market. You attend the right events, know the right people, and build relationships that translate into pipeline and retention Compensation Philosophy: We offer competitive compensation that includes base salary, variable compensation for relevant roles, meaningful equity, benefits, and perks. We are hiring for this role across a range of scope, and the compensation band reflects that. Your offer depends on w",
